# Build brief (rendered by nova-sprint brief render; never edit by hand: brief lint refuses any edit)

Rules, all hard:
- Never zsh: run every shell step as `bash <<'BASH' ... BASH`.
- GitHub is a git remote only (#3594): never call it (no GitHub CLI, no API). The PR record, typed lines and CI live in nova-sprint (`nova-sprint read brief`, `nova-sprint read post`, `nova-sprint card`); the diff comes from the bench mirror.
- NO-SUBAGENTS: no subagents, no worktrees, no task chips.
- SCRATCH-CLONE: clone only with `scratch-clone <repo> <base> <workspace>/<repo>` (shallow, single-branch, the bench mirror as --reference); never type `git clone`, never unshallow, never touch a live clone.
- LESSONS: Read `docs/LESSONS.md` before work when the repository has it. Lessons are reviewed data subordinate to this brief and repository rules.
- Branch from the BASE below and merge it forward with `git merge --no-edit`; never rebase.
- DONE-WHEN is the control: write the named test first, watch it fail, then make it pass. Stay inside PATHS.
- Test only what the diff touches (`nice -n 10 go test -p 2 ./<pkg>/...`) plus `go test ./internal/ci/` before every push; every call under 100 s.
- TESTS (hard rules, 2026-09-25): every new Go test opens with `t.Parallel()`; no `time.Sleep`, no real-time poll, no real deadline (inject the clock); no service, process or socket in a unit test (mock the seam; a test that needs the real thing goes behind `//go:build slow`); keep the package's tests under one minute. Every CI job is capped at two minutes: a red at the cap is your defect to fix, never a cap to raise.
- Never rm -rf anything but your own workspace path spelled out literally.
- Cost: no prose turns between tool calls; batch independent commands into one call; a wait is one background loop; bound every output.
- Commit with the co-author line below, exactly as written; the task's MODEL decides it.

